<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Almaty airport re-opens after runway repair.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Almaty airport re-opens after runway repair.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The international airport in Kazakhstan's capital Almaty reopened on Friday after 11 days of repairs, an aviation official said.</p>
<p>A Kazakhstan Aviation Agency spokesman said that Lufthansa had finished the repairs, which had closed the facility's runways during the day and left them open only at night.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, (3272) 509410</p>
</text>
